 ## Background
-PBR-NeRF was introduced in the paper "PBR-NeRF: Inverse Rendering with Physics-Based Neural Fields" [S1]. It builds upon the NeILF/NeILF++ neural fields framework [44, 51] and addresses the limitation of existing NeRF and 3D Gaussian Splatting approaches that estimate view-dependent appearance without modeling scene materials and illumination [S1]. The method introduces two novel physics-based priors: Conservation of Energy and NDF-weighted Specular Losses, to better constrain the inverse rendering estimation [S1].
